{
  "title": "Curation Over Complexity",
  "text": [
    "I created Color Supply because most color picking tools overwhelm users with too many choices at once. While precision is useful for fine-tuning, it often gets in the way when you are starting a project from scratch.",
    "Instead of making users pick every single color manually, this tool provides smart starting points that can be refined as they go. This turns the \"math\" of color theory into a faster, more confident workflow."
  ]
},

     
    {
      "media": [
        {
          "name": "color_wheels.jpg",
          "position": "center"
        }
      ]
    },
{
  "title": "Visualizing Complex Rules",
  "text": [
    "The interface is built to turn abstract color rules into something you can feel. By interacting with the wheel, users see how different schemes like complementary or triadic work in real time.",
    "It replaces manual calculation with instant visual feedback, making it easier to experiment and find the right balance."
  ]
},
    {
      "media": [
        {
          "name": "triad.mp4",
          "position": "center"
        }
      ]
    },
 


{
  "title": "Built for Scale",
  "text": [
    "I built Color Supply to solve a real problem for myself, and it ended up finding a massive audience of designers, artists, and developers worldwide. That kind of reach has taught me that people really value clarity over complicated features. It’s rewarding to see it become a trusted part of the daily workflow for so many professionals."
  ]
},
